cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NQX-Core: Pre-silicon emulator and chip development kit for the NautilusQuant golden-ratio KV-cache accelerator"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Doronin"
    given-names: "Herman"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hermandoronin/NautilusQuant"
url: "https://github.com/hermandoronin/NautilusQuant"
abstract: >-
  NQX-Core is a software emulator of a domain-specific processor for the
  NautilusQuant pipeline (deterministic KV-cache quantization via golden-ratio
  rotations). It includes the full instruction set architecture, an assembler,
  a SystemVerilog RTL skeleton with placeholder datapaths in the polar and
  quantizer units, ASIC floorplan and timing closure documents,
  a FastAPI HTTP service with monitoring and chaos tests, a head-to-head
  benchmark against TurboQuant, and a pre-silicon SDK with Yosys synthesis,
  OpenLane configuration for Skywater 130nm MPW, and SymbiYosys formal
  verification.
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-04-30
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - LLM inference
  - KV-cache quantization
  - golden ratio
  - phi
  - dataflow accelerator
  - ASIC emulator
  - hardware-software co-design
  - NautilusQuant
